# Example apps live in examples/ and ARE tracked by this repo, so people can
# read the source without building them. Their build artifacts are not:
# each app's own .gitignore (node_modules/, .expo/, dist/, ...) applies to
# its own subtree, and the catch-alls below back that up.
#
# Apps you build for yourself in this workspace are a different case — they
# get their own isolated git repo (see the skill's build-flow.md) and should
# be listed here so this repo ignores them.

.DS_Store
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
*.tsbuildinfo
.env*.local

# Per-app agent state generated by the skill's validation loop. Regenerated
# from source on every run, machine-specific (screenshots differ by OS, GPU
# and font rendering), and meaningless in someone else's checkout — so it is
# never committed. Note this ignores generated state only: the skill itself,
# at .claude/skills/, is deliberately tracked.
**/.claude/app-map.json
**/.claude/design-constraints.json
**/.claude/logs/
**/.claude/visual/

# Claude Code writes per-developer permission grants here, and they contain
# absolute paths from whoever's machine approved them. Shared settings belong
# in .claude/settings.json; personal ones stay out of the repo.
.claude/settings.local.json
